---
import StepCard from '../StepCard.astro';
import ToolsOverview from '../diagrams/ToolsOverview.astro';
---

<div class="sec" id="s5">
  <div class="num">05</div>
  <h2>Zed for the full editor experience</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Zed is a fast code editor. Use it when you want to see every file and poke
    at things yourself.
  </p>
  <p>
    An editor is a program for opening and changing text files, which is what
    code is. Zed (<a href="https://zed.dev">zed.dev</a>) is a quick, clean one.
    Open your project folder in it and you get a file list down the side and the
    contents in the middle. You can also run Claude as an agent inside Zed,
    which is handy for small hands on tweaks.
  </p>
  <h3>Add Claude Agent to Zed</h3>
  <div class="steps">
    <StepCard number="1" title={'Install Zed and open your folder'}
      ><p>
        Download it from zed.dev, open it and choose your project folder.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="2" title={'Open the Agent Panel'}
      ><p>
        It is the panel for talking to agents inside Zed. There is a button for
        it in the corner of the window, or open it from the View menu.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="3" title={'Add an agent from the ACP Registry'}
      ><p>
        In the Agent Panel look for Add Agent, then Install from Registry and
        pick Claude Agent. ACP is the Agent Client Protocol, a shared language
        that lets editors like Zed talk to agents like Claude. The registry is
        the list of agents that speak it.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="4" title={'Sign in with /login'}
      ><p>
        Start a new thread with Claude Agent, type <code class="i">/login</code> and
        follow the prompts to sign in with your Claude account. The exact steps are
        on <a href="https://zed.dev/docs">zed.dev/docs</a> under External Agents.
      </p></StepCard
    >
  </div>
  <h3>Delta or Zed?</h3>
  <div class="two">
    <div class="card" style="border-color: var(--color-7dffa8)">
      <div class="num" style="color: var(--color-b8ffd0); margin-bottom: 8px">
        Delta
      </div><ul>
        <li>Planning a task</li><li>Reviewing what the agent did</li><li>
          Sharing a thread with me
        </li><li>Getting help when stuck</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="border-color: var(--color-ffb347)">
      <div class="num" style="margin-bottom: 8px">Zed</div><ul>
        <li>Browsing the files yourself</li><li>
          Small hands on tweaks (text, a colour)
        </li><li>Seeing the whole project at once</li><li>
          Opening a file the agent mentioned
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
    <ToolsOverview />
    <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-9ee6b5)">
      One engine, one folder, two windows onto it. Delta for the conversation
      and the review, Zed for the files.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
